{# Modern Template 10 — FinTech Elite · two-column · editorial sidebar, slider skills
   Ported from block <!-- 10 --> / id="t10" of "Resume Templates Coded.dc.html".
   Locked spec: burnt-orange #A93005 sidebar (280px, white text) on a white
   body. Sidebar: circular portrait, centred Archivo 900 name + tracked title,
   Phone / Email / Location / … contact blocks, then Tools, Languages and
   Certifications under Poppins 700 24px labels. Body (Archivo 900 24px section
   heads): SUMMARY, a four-chip stat band (1px #cfcfcf rules, blue #0369a1
   numerals), EXPERIENCE, EDUCATION, and SKILLS — one #cfcfcf rounded card
   holding a 3-column grid of slider rows (track #d5e8f5, fill #38bdf8, a white
   knob ringed in #38bdf8) with the percent/level as real text.

   Divergences from the supplied reference:
     1. Palette — sidebar #A93005 + body blue #0369a1 / #38bdf8, locked here.
     2. The reference lists skills twice (a plain sidebar "Key Skills" list and
        the body sliders); the data model has one `skills` list, so it renders
        once as the body sliders. The sidebar slot carries Tools instead.
     3. Contact icon/label blocks keep the label as real text; LinkedIn etc.
        come from `contact.social`.
     4. The reference splits the 9 sliders into three bordered cards; the data
        model has a variable skill count, so it renders as one bordered card
        with an internal 3-column slider grid (last row simply partial).
     5. `.tpl` is a plain flex two-column; body gap 26->30 opened to seat the
        lighter shared sample.

   ROOT FAMILY -- KNOWN EXCEPTION, deliberately left as it is.
   'DM Sans' is not vendored in fonts.css, not on the FONTS.md allowlist, and
   has no Arabic alias in fetch_fonts_ar.py::PAIRINGS. So this root falls back
   to the browser's default sans in Latin -- which differs between Windows and
   macOS -- and to whatever the OS supplies in Arabic, making t10 the one
   template of 49 the Arabic font work does not reach. The pixel golden was
   captured WITH that fallback, so the baseline agrees with it.

   It was changed to Inter and changed back on 2026-09-20: fixing it moves this
   template's ENGLISH pixels, and the standing instruction is that the Arabic
   font policy must not alter English CV templates. An Arabic-only fix is not
   available -- the alias generator only emits rules for families present in
   fonts.css, so a family absent there cannot be given Arabic coverage without
   also making it render in English.
   tests/test_template_fonts.py carries this as a named exemption. #}
{% import "_macros.j2" as m %}
{% set SLAB = "font-family:Poppins,sans-serif; font-weight:700; font-size:22px; margin-bottom:14px;" %}
{% set BH = "font-family:Archivo,sans-serif; font-weight:900; font-size:24px; color:#111111; letter-spacing:-0.3px;" %}
<div class="tpl cv-sections-taj" style="box-sizing:border-box; width:850px; height:1100px; display:flex; background:#ffffff; font-family:'DM Sans',sans-serif; color:#111111;">

  <div style="width:280px; flex-shrink:0; background:#A93005; color:#ffffff; padding:42px 32px; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:26px; box-sizing:border-box;">
    <div style="width:148px; height:148px; flex-shrink:0; border-radius:50%; background:#d5d8dd; align-self:center; overflow:hidden; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; font-size:11px; color:#6a6a6a;">
      {% if r.photo_url %}<img src="{{ r.photo_url }}" alt="" style="width:100%; height:100%; object-fit:cover; display:block;">{% else %}{{ t('PHOTO') }}{% endif %}
    </div>
    <div style="text-align:center;">
      <div class="cv-name" style="font-family:Archivo,sans-serif; font-weight:900; font-size:38px; line-height:1.02; letter-spacing:-1px;">{{ r.name }}</div>
      {% if r.title %}<div style="font-weight:700; font-size:15px; opacity:0.92; letter-spacing:1px; text-transform:uppercase; margin-top:8px;">{{ r.title }}</div>{% endif %}
    </div>

    {% set c = r.contact %}
    {% if c.phone or c.email or c.address or c.site or c.social %}
    <div style="display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:16px;">
      {% if c.phone %}<div><div style="font-weight:700; font-size:14px; margin-bottom:2px;">{{ t('Phone') }}</div><div style="font-size:12.5px; opacity:0.88;">{{ c.phone }}</div></div>{% endif %}
      {% if c.email %}<div><div style="font-weight:700; font-size:14px; margin-bottom:2px;">{{ t('Email') }}</div><div style="font-size:12.5px; opacity:0.88; overflow-wrap:anywhere;">{{ c.email }}</div></div>{% endif %}
      {% if c.address %}<div><div style="font-weight:700; font-size:14px; margin-bottom:2px;">{{ t('Location') }}</div><div style="font-size:12.5px; opacity:0.88;">{{ c.address }}</div></div>{% endif %}
      {% if c.site %}<div><div style="font-weight:700; font-size:14px; margin-bottom:2px;">{{ t('Website') }}</div><div style="font-size:12.5px; opacity:0.88; overflow-wrap:anywhere;">{{ c.site }}</div></div>{% endif %}
      {% for s in c.social %}{% if s.label or s.url %}<div>{% if s.label %}<div style="font-weight:700; font-size:14px; margin-bottom:2px;">{{ s.label }}</div>{% endif %}{% if s.url %}<div style="font-size:12.5px; opacity:0.88; overflow-wrap:anywhere;">{{ s.url }}</div>{% endif %}</div>{% endif %}{% endfor %}
    </div>
    {% endif %}

    {% if r.tools %}
    <div>
      <div class="cv-section" style="{{ SLAB }}">{{ t('Tools') }}</div>
      <div style="display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:8px; font-size:13px; line-height:1.35;">
        {% for tool in r.tools %}<div>{{ tool }}</div>{% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
    {% endif %}

    {% if r.languages %}
    <div>
      <div class="cv-section" style="{{ SLAB }}">{{ t('Languages') }}</div>
      <div style="display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:9px; font-size:13px;">
        {% for l in r.languages %}
        <div style="display:flex; justify-content:space-between; gap:8px;"><span>{{ l.name }}</span><span style="font-weight:700;">{{ l.level }}</span></div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
    {% endif %}

    {% if r.recognition %}
    <div>
      <div class="cv-section" style="{{ SLAB }}">{{ t('Certifications') }}</div>
      <div style="display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:11px; font-size:13px; line-height:1.4;">
        {% for rec in r.recognition %}
        <div>{{ rec.title }}{% if rec.detail %}<div style="font-weight:700; font-size:12.5px;">{{ rec.detail }}</div>{% endif %}</div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>

  <div style="flex:1; min-width:0; padding:46px 42px; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:38px; box-sizing:border-box;">
    {% if r.summary %}
    <div>
      <div class="cv-section" style="{{ BH }}">{{ t('SUMMARY') }}</div>
      <p style="font-size:13px; color:#333333; line-height:1.65; margin:14px 0 0;">{{ r.summary }}</p>
    </div>
    {% endif %}

    {% if r.achievements %}
    <div style="display:grid; grid-auto-flow:column; grid-auto-columns:minmax(0,1fr); gap:12px; border-top:1px solid #cfcfcf; border-bottom:1px solid #cfcfcf; padding:14px 0;">
      {% for a in r.achievements %}
      {% if a.metric %}
      <div style="text-align:center;">
        <div style="font-family:Archivo,sans-serif; font-weight:900; font-size:25px; line-height:1; color:#0369a1;">{{ a.metric }}</div>
        <div style="font-size:9px; letter-spacing:1px; font-weight:700; text-transform:uppercase; color:#666666; margin-top:5px;">{{ a.label }}</div>
      </div>
      {% endif %}
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
    {% endif %}

    {% if r.experience %}
    <div>
      <div class="cv-section" style="{{ BH }}">{{ t('EXPERIENCE') }}</div>
      <div style="display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:16px; margin-top:14px;">
        {% for job in r.experience %}
        <div>
          <div style="display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:baseline; gap:12px;">
            <div style="font-weight:700; font-size:16px; color:#111111;">{{ job.role }}</div>
            {% if job.start or job.end %}<div style="font-size:12.5px; color:#333333; white-space:nowrap;">{{ job.start }}{% if job.start and job.end %} – {% endif %}{{ job.end }}</div>{% endif %}
          </div>
          {% if job.company or job.location %}<div style="font-size:13px; color:#333333; margin:2px 0 6px;">{{ job.company }}{% if job.company and job.location %} · {{ job.location }}{% elif job.location %}{{ job.location }}{% endif %}</div>{% endif %}
          {% if job.bullets %}
          <ul style="margin:0; padding-inline-start:18px; font-size:12.5px; color:#333333; line-height:1.5;">
            {% for b in job.bullets %}<li>{{ b }}</li>{% endfor %}
          </ul>
          {% endif %}
        </div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
    {% endif %}

    {% if r.education %}
    <div>
      <div class="cv-section" style="{{ BH }}">{{ t('EDUCATION') }}</div>
      <div style="display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:12px; margin-top:14px;">
        {% for ed in r.education %}
        <div>
          <div style="display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:baseline; gap:12px;">
            <div style="font-weight:700; font-size:15px; color:#111111;">{{ ed.degree }}</div>
            {% if ed.start or ed.end %}<div style="font-size:12.5px; color:#333333; white-space:nowrap;">{{ ed.start }}{% if ed.start and ed.end %} - {% endif %}{{ ed.end }}</div>{% endif %}
          </div>
          {% if ed.school %}<div style="font-size:13px; color:#333333;">{{ ed.school }}{% if ed.gpa %} · {{ t('GPA') }} {{ ed.gpa }}{% endif %}</div>{% endif %}
        </div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
    {% endif %}

    {% if r.skills %}
    <div>
      <div class="cv-section" style="{{ BH }}">{{ t('SKILLS') }}</div>
      <div style="margin-top:14px; border:1px solid #cfcfcf; border-radius:8px; padding:18px 20px; display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr)); gap:16px 22px;">
        {% for sk in r.skills %}
        {{ m.skill_slider(sk, {'track': '#d5e8f5', 'fill': '#38bdf8', 'row_min': 32}) }}
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</div>
